{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>From every beast and from every wild animal of the field.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): just as you are more cunning than every wild animal of the field, so shall you be more cursed than every beast. And so our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: ערום מכל — ארור מכל, 'more cunning than all — more cursed than all.'" "<b>And by way of </b>the Midrash, our Rabbis, of blessed memory, proved from here the gestation period of the serpent: seven years. This is what our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded in tractate Bekhorot: מכל הבהמה ומכל חית השדה — if from beast he was cursed, from wild animal how much the more so; from here follows that the gestation period of the serpent is seven years. And the explanation of the matter is that Scripture should have properly placed the lesser first and then the greater; now the gestation period of a wild animal is fifty-two days, which is one-seventh of that of a beast, whose gestation period is twelve months. Therefore Scripture placed beast before wild animal, to make known that just as the beast was cursed by seven parts relative to the wild animal, so the serpent was cursed by seven parts relative to the beast. And R. Yehoshua proved this in the Talmud for that sectarian from this verse, and the sectarian did not believe until he tested the matter and found it according to his words, and the sectarian struck his head against the ground." "<b>On your belly you shall go and dust you shall eat.</b> Measure for measure: He lowered them from their rank and brought them down to the dust — therefore He diminished his stature and gave him dust as food. And He did not mention in his curse that he be stricken mute, for the curse of muteness would have been harshest of all, and therefore it would have been fitting to punish him with it. But the serpent was a body prepared for punishment, as Scripture testified: ערום מכל חית השדה — and it was a vessel to receive the force bound within it, for what was revealed and what was hidden in it are truth. And HaShem, who diminished his stature, likewise diminished the force bound within it, bringing it down below the sefirot, which are three sets of three — for He is not an El who delights in wickedness, evil does not sojourn with Him, and therefore it is banished from all of them, from the three camps of above — in the manner of the metzora, who is banished from the three camps of below." "<b>And you already </b>know that that force began to speak slander against its Creator; therefore it was stricken with tzara'at and banished from its rank. And understand this. From here our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said always, concerning all who speak what is unfitting or counsel advice that is improper: עפרא בפומיה — 'dust in his mouth,' as they said: עפרא בפומיה דאיוב — 'dust in the mouth of Job,' and this is the fitting punishment for all who incite." "<b>All the days of your life.</b> This tells that this punishment shall never depart from him, even in the days of the Messiah, when the enmity between the woman and the serpent shall be removed, in the manner of what is written (Isaiah 11:8): ושעשע יונק על חור פתן — this punishment, of eating dust, shall never depart from him at all; as it is written (Isaiah 65:25): זאב וטלה ירעו כאחד ואריה כבקר יאכל תבן ונחש עפר לחמו. Therefore it says 'all the days of your life,' to allude to the days of the Messiah, in the manner that our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded it regarding the exodus from Egypt (Deuteronomy 16:3): למען תזכור את יום צאתך מארץ מצרים כל ימי חייך — 'ימי חייך' — this world; 'כל ימי חייך' — to bring the days of the Messiah. And so we may bring it here as well."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:09:53.533689721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}